{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"ddead267b6c8fa96fe678d67a6f82cc42fbdc4bc1bc584c1a8a9a51e9169cd56","slug":"medium-mixtures","location":"/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Medium Mixtures","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info/blob/main/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info/edit/main/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","thumbnail":"/build/mixed_medium-9e2b5c33de4ad0e7e1fd070edf1fbe2a.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"medium_mixtures.md","url":"/build/medium_mixtures-77cc7d72105666cc6cbead95ccd618af.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The 223 standard includes a large set of enumerations, defined as a hierarchy of subclasses under the class ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"tY8AMqCAz1"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:EnumerationKind","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"lGz2K5ACB9"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind","key":"hJMIdiJwSp"},{"type":"text","value":".\nOne important piece of this hierarchy is the class ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"jj4IVPHDKk"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"q2jtLfAFLA"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","key":"K8VTANmndi"},{"type":"text","value":" and its direct subclass ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"pv2riahNKb"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"p4zuZ8lRbW"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","key":"qHIMRsxOkT"},{"type":"text","value":".\nIt is this branch of the hierarchy where you can find what you would expect to be flowing in a building, such as water, air and electricity. It is important to understand how a medium is modeled, especially when that medium is a mixture. The diagram below sketches the structure of the hierarchy. The names of the classes are abbreviated for clarity, so ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"GYdbbdaYDU"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Ac3gS7PyCz"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","key":"ZvvVGXElX3"},{"type":"text","value":" is shown as Medium for example. In the standard, each of the names follows the hyphenated naming convention of <parent class>-<local class>.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"T6QE3GfHqG"}],"key":"toC8zarK2S"},{"type":"image","url":"/build/mixed_medium-9e2b5c33de4ad0e7e1fd070edf1fbe2a.png","alt":"MixedMedium","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"PIfTMAvL4K","urlSource":"images/mixed_medium.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note in the figure that there is a division of the Medium class into Mix and Constituent. The Mix class is further divided into Fluid and Power&Signal. Fluid means what you might think - a liquid or gas that typically flows inside some sort of conduit like a duct or a pipe. You can find Water and Air here. To capture the description of what is in a mixture, the model contains the class Constituent and its subclasses. These subclasses are intended to identify the constituents of a mixture. So, for example, a water-glycol mixture would be defined as ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"ZncPdAUiWB"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Water-GlycolSolution","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Water-GlycolSolution","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"PKiEORDcqH"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Water-GlycolSolution","key":"RcHx59wJKK"},{"type":"text","value":", with two Properties via the relation ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"z4S30x4iNV"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:composedOf","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:composedOf","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"rhVffl7gj5"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:composedOf","key":"d5eZYp5daw"},{"type":"text","value":". Each of these Properties has a relation ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"ErXC6kc7Wr"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:ofConstituent","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:ofConstituent","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"AZoAErBa60"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:ofConstituent","key":"wTWsgSzSDH"},{"type":"text","value":" that identifies one of the constituents from the Medium-Constituent hierarchy. Each Property also captures any other defining information. This is illustrated in the following figure for a 30%  Water-Glycol mixture.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"JIfxdJO7Ub"}],"key":"W5asvuNaIa"},{"type":"image","url":"/build/glycol_example-61e8e783097dc4ef2092891d0feb2db9.png","alt":"GlycolExample","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"yByrmvkTVo","urlSource":"images/glycol_example.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mixtures (","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"yb876plDkP"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Mix","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Medium-Mix","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"V1aardmJZx"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Mix","key":"e9cBXWrirG"},{"type":"text","value":") and constituents (","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"gq9XVeTQxV"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Constituent","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Medium-Constituent","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"CD4aT6eYZv"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Constituent","key":"JNBogsindA